   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Acts 1:8 names Jerusalem, Judea and Samaria, and \"the uttermost part of the earth.\" Trace where the story is in chapters 2, 8, 10 and 28. How does the book follow that map?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What question brought the apostles and elders together in Acts 15:1-6, and how does the phrase \"it seemed good to the Holy Spirit, and to us\" (15:28) describe the way they reached a decision?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/acts-of-the-apostles/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:acts-of-the-apostles"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Acts ends with Paul under guard in Rome yet preaching \"with all boldness, none forbidding him\" (28:31). Why might Luke end there rather than with Paul's trial, and what does that say about the ongoing story the church still lives in?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 4:36-37, what was Barnabas's real name, where was he from, and what did he do with his field?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Acts 9:26-27, why were the disciples in Jerusalem afraid of Saul, and what did Barnabas tell the apostles about him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Barnabas see when he arrived in Antioch (Acts 11:22-24), and how did he respond?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare the order of the names in Acts 13:2 and 13:7 with Acts 13:46. What change in the mission does it hint at?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/barnabas/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:barnabas"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Barnabas gave Mark a second chance after Mark had left the work (Acts 15:36-39). Who in your church or life might need someone to vouch for them, and what would it cost you to do it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 24:44, which three groups of writings does the risen Jesus say speak about him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does 2 Peter 3:15-16 describe Paul's letters, and what does that suggest about how early Christians regarded them?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why might it matter that the canon was recognised gradually by the whole church, rather than chosen in a single meeting?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/biblical-canon/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:biblical-canon"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "If your Bible has fewer or more Old Testament books than a friend's from another tradition, how could you talk about the difference with charity and accuracy?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Ezra 1:1-4 with 2 Chronicles 36:22-23. What do the two passages share, and what does that suggest about how the story of Israel continues after the exile?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Ezra 3:10-13, why do some people shout for joy while older priests and Levites weep at the laying of the Temple's foundation?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What stopped the rebuilding in Ezra 4:24, and according to Ezra 6:14, through whose prophesying did the elders build and prosper?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Ezra 7:10 says Ezra set his heart to seek the law, to do it and to teach it. Why do you think the order of those three verbs matters for anyone who studies Scripture?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/book-of-ezra/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:book-of-ezra"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Ezra's prayer in chapter 9 confesses the sins of the whole community, not just his own. What might it look like for a church to pray that way today?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "How does God describe himself to Moses in Exodus 34:6-7, and what does that tell us about where forgiveness begins?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 18:21-35, how large is the first servant's debt compared with what his fellow servant owes him, and what point is Jesus making by the contrast?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke 17:3-4 speaks of rebuking a brother who sins and forgiving him when he repents. How does that fit with Jesus praying for those crucifying him in Luke 23:34?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Joseph's forgiveness of his brothers in Genesis 50:15-21 include, and what did it not pretend?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/forgiveness-in-the-bible/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:forgiveness-in-the-bible"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Is there someone I find hard to forgive? What would it look like to begin by praying for them, even before my feelings change?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Matthew 1:1 calls Jesus \"the son of David, the son of Abraham.\" Why might Matthew open with those two names in particular?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Find the sentence that closes each of the five teaching blocks (Matthew 7:28, 11:1, 13:53, 19:1 and 26:1). What does each discourse teach disciples about life in the kingdom?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 5:17-20, what does Jesus say he came to do with the Law and the Prophets, and what kind of righteousness does he ask of his followers?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/gospel-of-matthew/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:gospel-of-matthew"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The Gospel begins with \"God with us\" (1:23) and ends with \"I am with you always\" (28:20). How does that promise frame everything in between, and where do you need to hear it this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Exodus 34:6 is God's own description of himself to Moses. Which words in it describe grace, and why is it striking that this comes right after the golden calf?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Ephesians 2:8-10, what saves us, what does not, and what are we then created for?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Romans 6:1-2, what wrong conclusion does Paul expect someone to draw from \"grace abounded\", and how does he answer it?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul hears \"My grace is sufficient for you\" in a time of weakness (2 Corinthians 12:9). Where in your own life, or your church's, do you most need grace as strength rather than only as pardon?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/grace/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:grace"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Each Christian tradition says that salvation begins with God's grace. How might that shared conviction change the way you talk with Christians of another tradition?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Mark 1:14-15, what does Jesus announce when he begins preaching in Galilee, and what two responses does he ask for?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Luke 11:20, what does Jesus point to as a sign that God's Kingdom \"has come to you\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What do the parables of the seed growing by itself and the mustard seed (Mark 4:26-32) suggest about how God's Kingdom grows, and who makes it grow?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Psalm 145:13 calls God's Kingdom everlasting, yet Jesus teaches us to pray \"Let your Kingdom come\" (Matthew 6:10). How can both be true?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/kingdom-of-god/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:kingdom-of-god"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "When you pray the Lord's Prayer, where in your own life, family or church do you most long to see God's will done \"as in heaven, so on earth\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Matthew 6:9-13 with Luke 11:2-4. Which petitions do both share, and what setting does each Gospel give the prayer (Matthew 6:5-8; Luke 11:1)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The first petitions are about God's name, kingdom and will; the later ones about our bread, our sins and our testing. What does that order teach about how to pray?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Every pronoun in the prayer is plural (\"our\", \"us\"). How does praying it change if I picture my church, or the believers I find hardest to love, praying it with me?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 6:14-15 Jesus adds a comment on just one petition. Which one, and why might he single it out?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/lords-prayer/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:lords-prayer"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus prays \"your desire be done\" in Gethsemane (Matthew 26:42). How does that scene deepen what it means to pray \"your will be done\"?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "What did Paul see in Athens that \"stirred\" his spirit (Acts 17:16), and where did he go to talk with people (17:17)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Why did some listeners think Paul was proclaiming \"strange gods\" (17:18)? What two things had he been preaching?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul quotes a Greek poet in Acts 17:28. What point does he draw from the line in the next verse (17:29)?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "The speech begins with creation and ends with repentance, judgment and the resurrection (17:30-31). Why do you think Paul builds toward Jesus in that order for this audience?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul-at-the-areopagus/check/5",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul-at-the-areopagus"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Luke records three responses in 17:32-34. Which response do you see most often when you talk about faith with friends or colleagues, and what might Paul's example teach you about those conversations?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Acts 9:1-6, what is Saul doing when Jesus meets him, and what question does Jesus ask him?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Compare Acts 9:20-30 with Galatians 1:15-24. What does each account emphasise about what Paul did after his conversion?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Philippians 3:4-8, which credentials does Paul list, and how does he now value them?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/paul/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:paul"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Paul calls himself \"the least of the apostles\" yet says God's grace was not in vain (1 Corinthians 15:9-10). How might his story shape the way we see people who have done harm, or our own past?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Acts 23:6-8, which beliefs did the Pharisees hold that the Sadducees rejected?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "In Matthew 23:2-3, what does Jesus tell the crowds to do with the Pharisees' teaching, and what does he warn them not to copy?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Nicodemus (John 3:1-2) and Gamaliel (Acts 5:34-39) were both Pharisees. How do their stories complicate the picture of the Pharisees as simply Jesus's enemies?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/pharisees/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:pharisees"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Jesus's sharpest warnings were aimed at devout, Bible-loving people. Where might Matthew 23:23-28 speak to our own church life today?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/1",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "According to Jeremiah 29:1-10, who first received the letter containing verse 11, where were they, and how long did God say they would wait?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/2",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Read Philippians 4:10-14. What \"all things\" is Paul talking about in verse 13, and how does that change the way the verse is often used?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/3",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Revelation 3:20 is often used in evangelism. To whom is it first addressed (Revelation 3:14-22), and what does that add to its meaning?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/check/4",
   "@type": "bgo:StudyQuestion",
   "bgo:questionFor": {
    "@id": "bg:reading-in-context"
   },
   "rdfs:label": "Which verse do you hold dear but have never read in its surrounding chapter, and what do you notice when you read the whole chapter this week?"
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/example",
   "@type": "bgo:Rewrite",
   "bgo:after": "God told exiles in Babylon to settle in and seek the city's peace, promising a future after seventy years; I can trust his good purposes and be faithful where I am, even if this interview fails.",
   "bgo:before": "God has promised me success and no setbacks, so this interview is bound to work out.",
   "bgo:situation": "A friend facing a job interview posts Jeremiah 29:11 as a guarantee that everything will go well.",
   "bgo:why": "Reading the whole letter (Jeremiah 29:1-14) shows a promise of long-range hope to a community in exile, which still comforts believers today but not as a pledge of quick personal success."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto",
   "@type": "schema:HowTo",
   "schema:name": "Reading in Context",
   "schema:step": [
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6"
    },
    {
     "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/1",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 1,
   "schema:text": "Read the whole paragraph, and then the whole chapter, around the verse before deciding what it means."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/2",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 2,
   "schema:text": "Ask who is speaking, to whom, and in what situation; note what the book itself tells you about its author and first readers."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/3",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 3,
   "schema:text": "Trace the flow of thought by asking what comes just before, what comes just after, and how the verse fits the argument or story."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/4",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 4,
   "schema:text": "Identify the kind of writing (letter, poem, prophecy, narrative) and read it the way that kind of writing is meant to be read."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/5",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 5,
   "schema:text": "Use a study Bible or Bible dictionary to fill in historical and cultural background, without letting the background drown out the text."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/6",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 6,
   "schema:text": "Compare the passage with other Scripture on the same subject, especially clearer passages, and see how it fits the whole story that centres on Christ."
  },
  {
   "@id": "https://github.com/john1hsu/bible-graph/id/reading-in-context/howto/7",
   "@type": "schema:HowToStep",
   "schema:position": 7,
   "schema:text": "Only then ask what the passage means for you or your church, applying it in a way its first readers would recognise as faithful to it."
  },
